tion-only`. It caps contributions from people lobbying on a matter, which the annex treats as a narrow ban, not \"strictly limit corporate and dark-money spending.\"\n- **Other passages:** his opposition to Proposition 4 (public financing) is `adjacent` / `off-axis`, because it is about taxpayer money, not limits on private money. The PG&E page's remarks on donations are `rhetorical`. His fundraising totals in the interview are his own conduct, so `adjacent`.\n- **`needs_source`:** two items. First, Hilton's own first-person words on contribution or spending limits from the 2026 campaign. Second, the *Positive Populism* (2018) passage on banning \"Conflict Donors\". The campaign page only paraphrases it.\n- **Quote:** I tiered \"Steve will extend the $500 limit to the Legislature.\" as `lever` / `lever-named` and marked it quotable. That sentence is the campaign page's wording, not his, so a reviewer may want to drop it from quotes.\n\nSeparately, these connectors need authorising in claude.ai connector settings before they can be used: Benevity, Candid, Canva, Figma, Harvey and WorkOS. The GitHub plugin also failed to connect (bad authorisation header). This task didn't need any of them.","ttft_ms":16311,"type":"result","duration_ms":37544,"uuid":"d6303295-36b9-434d-89bc-75c261a8d67a","ttft_stream_ms":1577,"time_to_request_ms":481,"first_content_frame_ms":1578,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
